<title>CANADA: GOLF-LEADING SCORES AFTER FINAL ROUND OF CANADIAN OPEN.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING SCORES AFTER FINAL ROUND OF CANADIAN OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>OAKVILLE, Ontario 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scores after</p>
<p>Sunday's final round of the Bell Canadian Open, shortened to</p>
<p>54 holes because of rain at the 7,112-yard, par-72 Glen Abbey</p>
<p>course (golfers U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>202 Dudley Hart 68 64 70</p>
<p>203 David Duval 69 65 69</p>
<p>205 Tom Byrum 70 66 69, Taylor Smith 68 66 71, Scott Dunlap</p>
<p>64 65 76</p>
<p>206 Michael Bradley 70 64 72</p>
<p>207 Tom Lehman 69 70 68, Mark Calcavecchia 71 68 68, Joey</p>
<p>Sindelar 70 68 69, Jesper Parnevik (Sweden) 66 71 70</p>
<p>208 Tiger Woods 70 70 68</p>
<p>209 Loren Roberts 69 71 69, Carl Paulson 67 72 70, Billy</p>
<p>Andrade 70 68 71</p>
<p>210 Bruce Lietzke 72 69 69, Guy Hill 67 74 69, Vijay Singh</p>
<p>(Fiji) 69 71 70, Andrew Magee 67 72 71, Jim Gallagher 71 67 72</p>
<p>211 Ernie Els (South Africa) 67 74 70, Billy Mayfair 67 72</p>
<p>72, Mark O'Meara 74 65 72, Emlyn Aubrey 69 69 73, Bob Tway 69</p>
<p>69 73, Frank Lickliter 67 69 75</p>
<p>Other foreigners:</p>
<p>214 Trevor Dodds (Namibia) 69 72 73, Stuart Appleby</p>
<p>(Australia) 70 71 73, Grant Waite (New Zealand) 69 72 73,</p>
<p>Frank Nobilo (New Zealand) 70 71 73</p>
<p>218 Fulton Allem (South Africa) 71 73 74, Anders Forsbrand</p>
<p>(Sweden) 70 74 74</p>
